codex
I selected `gated_delta_net_q8_fast`: it has the fewest recorded attempts among viable active kernels and is low-occupancy/L2-resident (16.5% occupancy, 31.8% memory busy, 64 VGPR, 2 KiB LDS). The untried hypothesis is to compute the per-head `exp(gate)` once in lane 0 and broadcast it, avoiding 31 redundant transcendental evaluations per token while leaving arithmetic and results unchanged.
