I selected `fused_rmsnorm_mq_rotate` for the one certification: its 0.1% occupancy is structural (one 256-thread block over 64 CUs), so register/unroll changes have already proven harmful. The variant only starts gfx12-only cache hints for the two reusable sign vectors during the independent RMS pass; it preserves all arithmetic, reductions, and consuming loads.
