`fused_rmsnorm_mq_rotate` is the least-attempted viable target. It is structurally under-occupied (one 256-thread block at decode), so extra prefetch/unrolling has already failed by raising VGPRs. I’ll instead remove redundant sign-table global loads: one warp will load the two 256-float sign tables into already-allocated dynamic LDS, and all eight warps will broadcast from LDS after the existing barrier. This preserves arithmetic and adds no new synchronization.
