The norm kernel is a single 256-thread block at decode, so global occupancy cannot be raised. I’m testing a gfx12-only scheduling change: issue each warp’s already-required first-group x/weight loads halfway through the unchanged sum-of-squares loop, giving them the remaining reductions as latency cover without changing arithmetic or any other architecture’s codegen.
