For residual, the certified dead changes all increased live state from 72 to 96 VGPRs and showed latency was already hidden. My distinct hypothesis is the opposite: split the current two-row wave into one row per wave, halving per-wave live headers/accumulators to recover occupancy without adding memory work per output element. The gfx12-only branch preserves other architectures’ compiled body verbatim.
