R7c1_weight_pk_u32x2_pair kernel=gemm_hfq4g256_moe_grouped_wmma_gfx12 lever=weight_pk_u32x2_pair verdict=DEAD delta_pct=0.31 f=0.594 learned=Pairing interleaved u32 weights kept VGPR at 64 while occupancy moved 92.9->92.3% and mem_busy 97.1->97.2%; same-byte traffic left this WMMA kernel saturated at the memory roofline.
R3c0_qkvza_xhoist32 kernel=fused_qkvza_hfq4g256 lever=xhoist32 verdict=DEAD delta_pct=0.32 f=0.5 learned=Hoisting group-quad x via float4 raised VGPR 72->88 and tanked L2 77.6->61.1% while occ/mem_busy stayed ~35%/41%; residual-style x-pre-DOG dual-issue does not unlock qkvza — TLP already hides x-load latency and extra live x vectors only add pressure without VALU throughput gain.
R11c3_qkv_k2048_specialize kernel=fused_qkv_hfq4g256 lever=qkv_k2048_specialize verdict=DEAD delta_pct=0.32 f=0.531 learned=Hard-specializing the hot K=2048 path raised VGPR 72->96 while occupancy stayed 53.6% and mem_busy 56.4%; TLP already hides latency, so removing dynamic loop/tail control adds register pressure without exposing a throughput lever.
R1c0_gup_w_mem_then_fma kernel=gemv_hfq4g256_moe_gate_up_k8_indexed lever=gup_w_mem_then_fma verdict=DEAD delta_pct=-5.1 f=0.0 learned=Separating weight VMEM from pure FMA (8 sc/zp/pk live with 32-wide x hoist) exploded VGPR 96->248 and DROPPED-WAVES occ 51.6->14.8% (wall share 12.5->16.1%); gate_up cannot afford residual-style w_preload — already at 96 VGPR with dual gate/up streams, so schedule reordering that extends header live ranges is closed; need a lever that cuts live state or improves L2 without holding more headers.
R8c1_down_meta_broadcast kernel=gemv_hfq4g256_moe_down_k8_indexed_batched_expanded lever=meta_broadcast verdict=DEAD delta_pct=-2.71 f=0.125 learned=Lane-0 scale/zero broadcast passed parity but lost 2.71%; profile_feedback was no clear lever signal with no variant counters, so duplicate header loads are not the exposed bottleneck and the kernel remains L2-resident/mixed-occupancy.
R2c0_res_perrow_wphase kernel=gemv_hfq4g256_residual lever=res_perrow_wphase verdict=DEAD delta_pct=1.29 f=0.625 learned=Per-row weight phases raised VGPR 72->96 (compiler kept more live) while occ only 26.6% and mem_busy 55.1%; TLP already hides latency so dual-row residual is NOT live-range/MLP limited — schedule splits that increase peak VGPR are closed.
R8c2_rms_k2048_phase2_ctrl kernel=fused_rmsnorm_mq_rotate lever=k2048_phase2_ctrl verdict=DEAD delta_pct=1.17 f=0.562 learned=K=2048 Phase-2 control specialization passed parity but produced no profile shift and failed dominance; with baseline occ 0.2%, mem_busy 18.0%, L2 73.7%, and VGPR 48, dynamic Phase-2 guards are not this one-block kernel's exposed latency.
R12c3_res_rowphase_preload4 kernel=gemv_hfq4g256_residual lever=res_rowphase_preload4 verdict=DEAD delta_pct=-0.10 f=0.438 learned=Row-local four-header preload phases unexpectedly raised VGPR 72->96; at 26.6% occupancy and 55.1% mem_busy, TLP already hides latency, so splitting the dual-row memory/FMA schedule does not relieve the real bottleneck.
R3c0_res_pair_stream kernel=gemv_hfq4g256_residual lever=res_pair_stream verdict=DEAD delta_pct=-0.09 f=0.528 learned=Half-quad pair stream (2 groups × 2 rows) kept VGPR at 72 and occ ~21% with mem_busy 40.9%/L2 77.9%; compiler did not free the expected live-range headroom, and TLP already hides latency so shrinking the x/header window is not residual's bottleneck.
