codex
The ledger rules out broadcasts and the packed-state transpose: raising occupancy/memory activity did not move decode. My distinct hypothesis is that the batch-1 decode path can keep each row’s four state values in registers through update, output, and requantization, removing the repeated LDS round-trips while preserving each row’s arithmetic and RNG order. I’ll guard it to gfx12 so other architectures compile the unchanged body.
