codex
I found a safe incremental experiment: combine the current packed-LDS state layout with a gfx12-only vector load of the four adjacent row scales. This is not any rejected lever; it tests whether reducing the four redundant scale-load issues per lane still helps once the LDS packing win is present. The arithmetic and all non-gfx12 code stay unchanged.
