The down-GEMV ledger is already saturated with 102 variants, including dead row-count, launch-bound, routing, prefetch, dequant, and reduction changes, so I won’t duplicate any of them. I’m switching to the less-explored RMSNorm/rotate kernel (24 records): its single-block decode launch is structurally under-occupied, so the experiment reduces repeated LDS reads of the published RMS scalar without adding global traffic or registers.
