   166	fi
   167	# ---- WIN -> ADVANCE THE SHARED BASELINE so EVERY worker (this arch, all worktrees) inherits it next round.
   168	#      Optimistic concurrency: build the win commit on the CURRENT baseline tip and CAS the ref forward under a
   169	#      per-arch commit lock. A same-kernel staleness guard rejects the advance if another worker already moved
   170	#      THIS kernel since we measured (our delta would be against a now-stale version of the file) -> re-measured
   171	#      next round against the advanced baseline. Cross-kernel wins stack optimistically (second-order interactions
