+// groups' x values are already hoisted, but the old schedule issued all four
+// group-0 DOGs before any group-1 DOG.  Pair the two independent cached
+// weight loads for each output row instead: g0(row) immediately followed by
+// g1(row).  This gives the instruction scheduler two group streams while
+// keeping each row's accumulator/FMA order (g0 then g1), live values, fold,
+// reduction, and stores identical.  No gfx12 intrinsic or shared source
+// change is introduced: this file is an experiment-only replacement.
 
