R18c0_res_lds_x_g256 kernel=gemv_hfq4g256_residual lever=res_lds_x_g256 verdict=DEAD delta_pct=-7.82 f=0.0 learned=LDS stage of per-group 256-x (1KB) passed parity but raised VGPR 72->96 (compiler kept stage temps + dual-row headers live) and wall 6.7->14.4% with occ 22.5->34.9 mem_busy 45.3->66.8 L2 77.6->85.4; profile_feedback=TLP already hides latency, NOT MLP-limited — residual is NOT VGPR/x-live-window limited; barrier+LDS tax dominates; LDS-x closed for residual (same failure mode as qkvza/down)
R26c3_down_scalar_hdr64 kernel=gemv_hfq4g256_moe_down_k8_indexed_batched_expanded lever=down_scalar_hdr64 verdict=DEAD delta_pct=-2.11 f=0.031 learned=Scalar s_load_b64 headers passed parity but kept VGPR=88 and occ roughly flat 42.5->43.4% while L2 hit rose 75.8->81.8% and mem_busy 43.5->45.5%; serialized SMEM waits regressed decode, so coalesced vector header loads are already latency-hidden and header bandwidth is not the bottleneck.
R19c2_down_sched_vmemx kernel=gemv_hfq4g256_moe_down_k8_indexed_batched_expanded lever=sched_vmemx verdict=DEAD delta_pct=0.69 f=0.602 learned=gfx12 VMEM scheduling hint raised VGPR 88->96 and changed occ/mem counters but had no clear gain; this L2-resident GEMV is not limited by this MLP/scheduling placement.
R19c0_res_x_pergroup kernel=gemv_hfq4g256_residual lever=res_x_pergroup verdict=DEAD delta_pct=0.03 f=0.469 learned=Per-group x+w stream (undo full-quad x-hoist + 8-header MEMORY phase) raised VGPR 72->96 and cut occ 22.5->20.5% with mem_busy 45.3->41.6% L2 77.6->78.1; profile_feedback=TLP already hides latency, NOT MLP-limited — residual is NOT limited by full-quad x live window; compiler expanded live ranges across scoped blocks, so this occupancy/VGPR lever is closed for residual (same TLP-hidden regime as LDS-x / unroll / w-inline)
