 succeeded in 0ms:
R30c0_qkvza_spref_nq544 kernel=fused_qkvza_hfq4g256 lever=qkvza_spref_nq544 verdict=DEAD delta_pct=0.69 f=0.611 learned=Retargeting gfx12 s_prefetch from +272 (mid-current-quad/gp2) to +544 (true next-quad base) passed parity but raised VGPR 72->88 with mem_busy~41.3%/occ~35.3% and L2 77.6->61.2%; profile_feedback=TLP already hides latency, NOT MLP-limited — qkvza is not limited by next-iteration weight-header miss placement; single-hint weight prefetch retarget (mid-quad vs next-quad) is closed on this L2-resident VALU-heavy GEMV
R31c0_qkvza_x_spref4 kernel=fused_qkvza_hfq4g256 lever=qkvza_x_spref4 verdict=DEAD delta_pct=0.6 f=0.583 learned=Gfx12 next-quad activation s_prefetch×4 (alongside existing weight +272) passed parity but raised VGPR 72->88, cut L2 hit 77.6->61.4%, left occ~35.6%/mem_busy~41.9%; profile_feedback=TLP already hides latency, NOT MLP-limited — qkvza scalar x[] stream is not a first-demand miss bottleneck; both weight-path and activation-path s_prefetch are closed on this L2-resident mixed GEMV
R1c2_lane0_header_bcast kernel=gemv_hfq4g256_multirow_r2 lever=lane0_header_bcast verdict=DEAD_FILE delta_pct=NA f=NA learned=BOD remains saturated (occ=89.3%, mem_busy=93.0%, vgpr=96); no variant profile was produced because the r2 entry aliases gemv_hfq4g256_multirow.hip and the certify harness cannot file-swap a two-way symbol mapping.
R1c3_qkvza_setprio1 kernel=fused_qkvza_hfq4g256 lever=qkvza_setprio1 verdict=DEAD delta_pct=-1.93 f=0.25 learned=Gfx12 wave-priority elevation at the existing weight-prefetch point passed exact-token parity but raised VGPR 72->88 and regressed decode while observed occ rose 35.1->48.0% and mem_busy 41.6->58.0%; TLP already hides the L2-resident latency, so scheduler-priority intervention adds pressure without exposing useful MLP and is closed for qkvza.
R32c0_down_rowmaj_dog kernel=gemv_hfq4g256_moe_down_k8_indexed_batched_expanded lever=down_rowmaj_dog verdict=DEAD delta_pct=-0.16 f=0.469 learned=Row-major DOG (r0g0,r0g1,...) passed parity but raised VGPR 88->96 with occ 42.5->41.4%, L2 75.8->71.6%, mem_busy~43.2% and profile_feedback=no clear lever signal; reordering independent DOGs for per-row weight L1 locality is not the limiter on this L2-resident multirow down GEMV — group-major vs row-major weight issue order is closed (TLP already hides latency; schedule of free DOGs does not move decode).
R33c0_down_x_spref8 kernel=gemv_hfq4g256_moe_down_k8_indexed_batched_expanded lever=down_x_spref8 verdict=DEAD delta_pct=-0.72 f=0.438 learned=8x gfx12 s_prefetch of full K=512 rot_batch x (256B lines) during routing setup passed parity but raised VGPR 88->96, cut occ 42.5->41.4 and L2 75.8->71.8 with mem_busy~42.9; profile_feedback=no clear lever signal. Activation first-demand misses are NOT the bottleneck on this L2-resident 4x2 down GEMV — x is already covered by the float4 hoist under TLP, and extra scalar prefs only add live-state/hint tax (weight g0 pref remains; full-window x-prefetch closed).
R2c3_down_g0_pref2frontier kernel=gemv_hfq4g256_moe_down_k8_indexed_batched_expanded lever=down_g0_pref2frontier verdict=DEAD delta_pct=0.59 f=0.608 learned=Removing the row2/row3 gfx12 group-0 prefetches from the shared four-row prefetch frontier passed exact-token coherence but remained unresolved below the DEAD threshold after 12 rounds with no profile counter shift; scalar prefetch issue count is not the limiter, and demand-loading the later two 272-byte row streams exposes no certifiable decode gain.
R1c1_grouped_wmma_u32x4_pair2 kernel=gemm_hfq4g256_moe_grouped_wmma_gfx12 lever=u32x4_pair2 verdict=DEAD delta_pct=0.03 f=0.438 learned=Two uint4 packed-weight loads passed exact-token parity but left VGPR=64 and mem_busy=97.2% with occupancy essentially flat at 92.4%; L2 fell 77.4->76.0%, so this grouped WMMA is already roofline-saturated and reducing VMEM instruction count did not expose throughput.
R2c2_rms_late_signs_gfx12 kernel=fused_rmsnorm_mq_rotate lever=rms_late_signs_gfx12 verdict=DEAD delta_pct=0.09 f=0.531 learned=Deferring both signs increased VGPR 48->56 while occupancy remained 0.2% (L2 71.1%, mem_busy 17.5%); the one-block grid is structurally under-occupied and sign live-range trimming did not create per-wave MLP.
R34c0_down_out_spref kernel=gemv_hfq4g256_moe_down_k8_indexed_batched_expanded lever=down_out_spref verdict=DEAD delta_pct=-2.2 f=0.062 learned=Early gfx12 s_prefetch of expert_outputs store window (with out_base hoist) passed parity but raised VGPR 88->96, shifted occ 42.5->63.9%, mem_busy 43.5->66.2%, L2 75.8->71.7%; profile_feedback=no clear lever signal and decode -2.2%. Write-allocate of the expanded-output pure-store is NOT the end-of-kernel bottleneck on this short L2-resident 4x2 down GEMV — extra output-prefetch traffic adds live-state/hint tax and pollutes the weight-resident cache window (store-path s_prefetch closed; keep weight g0_spref only).
R3c3_rms_pref_issue_schedbar kernel=fused_rmsnorm_mq_rotate lever=rms_pref_issue_schedbar verdict=DEAD delta_pct=-0.47 f=0.375 learned=Forcing the existing first-group x/weight/sign VMEM issue ahead of the reduction with a gfx12 scheduler barrier passed exact-token parity but raised VGPR 48->56 while structural occupancy stayed 0.2%, L2 fell 73.7->71.1%, and mem_busy stayed 18%; explicit issue ordering lengthens live ranges without creating usable MLP, so compiler scheduling fences are closed on this one-block kernel.
R35c0_rms_p1a_softpipe2 kernel=fused_rmsnorm_mq_rotate lever=rms_p1a_softpipe2 verdict=DEAD delta_pct=-0.47 f=0.469 learned=Phase-1a 2-deep soft-pipe raised VGPR 48->56 while occ stayed structurally 0.2% (wall 4.2%, L2 71.3%, mem_busy 17.7%); extra live v_cur/v_next does not create usable per-wave MLP on the one-block RMS path — same under-occ ceiling as 1-deep p1_pipe1; register-deepening p1a rings are closed, need launch-level parallelism or a register-neutral latency lever
