The profile resolves the apparent opportunity: this kernel is structurally one workgroup at decode, so its 0.1% occupancy cannot be raised by launch bounds. Its prior failures show that extra live values immediately collapse the already tiny wave pool. I’ll keep the 48-VGPR live range intact and test a distinct gfx12-only instruction-scheduling form rather than revisiting its failed prefetch/LDS/reduction levers.
